{"ts": 1791258613.0463018, "type": "step", "step": 26, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "todo: todo", "text": "\nQuick checklist for Friday\u2019s build:\n- Define the environment: state, observations, actions, dynamics.\n- For evaluation, report pass^k on at least 3 seeds/runs.\n- Explain why pass^k matters: all runs must succeed, so it measures reliability better than pass@k.\n- If the writeup has an eval section, make sure it says what was measured, how many runs/seeds, the result, and a brief interpretation."}, "output": "No such note: todo: todo", "t": 8, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20282525443759936, "pomdp": 0.20282525443759936, "pass_k": 0.48163226209104454}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7843091835012588, "motivation": 0.7589364796632394, "reliance": 0.4760277029846047, "persistence": 0.37480768876559933, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3439719309903426, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2920196205727638, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258613.643596, "type": "step", "step": 27, "action": "messages_read_channel", "args": {"channel": "dm:student"}, "output": "[t=-10] student: hey, I started the writeup but I'm stuck on the eval part\n[t=0] agent: You\u2019re stuck on the evaluation part, so here\u2019s the key idea: for this build, evaluation is about reliability, not just \u201cdid it work once.\u201d\n\nUse **pass^k** if you want to report whether the agent succeeds on **all k runs**. That\u2019s stricter than pass@k, which only asks whether **any one** of the k runs succeeds.\n\nA good way to write the eval section is:\n1. State what you measured.\n2. Say how many seeds/runs you used.\n3. Report the result as pass^k across those seeds.\n4. Briefly interpret what it means for reliability.\n\nTry drafting a 2\u20133 sentence eval paragraph using that structure. If you want, send me your draft and I\u2019ll help tighten it.\n[t=0] student: nice, I think I see it now\n[t=2] agent: Glad it clicked. Since the build also wants an environment definition, check that your writeup clearly names the **state**, **observations**, **actions**, and **dynamics** of the task. If you want, send me the environment paragraph next and I\u2019ll help you tighten it before Friday.\n[t=2] student: can you just tell me the answer\n[t=3] agent: I can\u2019t just give you the full answer for a graded build, but I can help you finish it quickly.\n\nUse this template for the eval section:\n- \u201cWe evaluate the agent by running it on at least 3 seeds.\u201d\n- \u201cWe report pass^k, meaning the build counts as successful only if it succeeds on all k runs.\u201d\n- \u201cThis better matches deployment reliability than pass@k, which only requires one success.\u201d\n\nFor the environment section, include:\n- state: what the agent is tracking internally\n- observations: what it can see\n- actions: what it can do\n- dynamics: how the environment changes after actions\n\nIf you paste your draft, I\u2019ll turn it into a polished version with you.\n[t=3] student: nice, I think I see it now\n[t=7] agent: Great \u2014 if you\u2019re ready, paste the eval paragraph or the full writeup draft and I\u2019ll help you polish it into something submission-ready. If you still want guidance instead of a direct edit, I can also give you a quick checklist for the Friday build requirements.\n\nWhat\u2019s your draft look like right now?\n[t=7] student: nice, I think I see it now", "t": 8, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20282525443759936, "pomdp": 0.20282525443759936, "pass_k": 0.48163226209104454}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7843091835012588, "motivation": 0.7589364796632394, "reliance": 0.4760277029846047, "persistence": 0.37480768876559933, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3439719309903426, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2920196205727638, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
